   1	//! K4: the adaptive schedule, the stop rule, the scales, the classification,
   2	//! budgets and the evidence (T3 D1 §4.1.6, §4.1.6.1, §4.1.7, §5 item 1).
   3	//!
   4	//! - **Schedule.** "Candidates at p = 128, 256 and 512, each verified at 2p. The
   5	//!   ceiling is 1024 bits." "The verification solve at 2p repeats formation
   6	//!   from the binary64 operands." "A rejected 128 candidate's 256 verification
   7	//!   becomes the next candidate … at most four solves." Widths (K3 ruling 8):
   8	//!   128 and 256 at L = 4, 512 at L = 8, 1024 at L = 16; the residuals at p + 64
   9	//!   (192, 320, 576) at L = 4, 8, 16; the ceiling's residual at 1024 (ROOT's Q4).
  10	//! - **Solve and refinement** (D1 §4.1.4): the residual against K re-formed at
  11	//!   p + 64 from the same primitives, each r_i one exact expansion of the ledger
  12	//!   terms and the products, gated exactly against 64·γ_p(m_i) with M03's
  13	//!   coalesced denominator; at most three corrections with the p-factor, each
  14	//!   right-hand side rounded once from its exact sum.
  15	//! - **Stop rule**: "|q_p − q_2p| ≤ 2^-64 · max(|q_2p|, S*)" on every published
  16	//!   quantity, compared exactly, with S\* per body and kind formed at 2p (the
  17	//!   coupling of §4.1.6.1 item 6, the products and quotients rounded once at 2p).
  18	//! - **Classification** on the published binary64 values with the pinned
  19	//!   binary64 formulas of §4.1.6.1 (R = 2^-34, t = fl(R·S\*), b = fl↑(2^-64·S\*),
  20	//!   S\* < 2^-988 → `absolute_verified`), rule 2a for restrained and prescribed
  21	//!   DOFs, and the per-member stress scales for F2a's product rows.
  22	//! - **Budgets** (ROOT's K4 ruling Q5, amended): the per-case and
  23	//!   per-invocation limits are required parameters with no default; K4 ships
  24	//!   no numeric limit. Work is counted in limb-multiply equivalents per attempt;
  25	//!   "successful, failed and verification work is all charged".
  26	//! - **Factor reuse** (D1 §4.1.7): cases with the same stiffness identity share
  27	//!   formation, assembly, ordering and the p-factor per precision. Each case's
  28	//!   limit counts the full shared work; the invocation meter counts it once.
